lly is just  the way he says things and the way he  just just oh look just a little look  from him tells you so much about this  guy his history and everything else the  other thing that could have been a real  brick around the movies next is Nova the  young human girl that and again in terms  of the overall there is the thing that  was a cool thing to get layered in which  I wasn't expecting because you know  people have said you know this is  actually a prequel to the original 60s  Planet of the Apes and I kind of I've  always approached that adds all  philosophically that's a neat idea I  don't know how cleanly it's kind of slot  in but they have act I mean you have to  disregard the latter um sequels to that  film because they come up with their own  origin for how the age Scott smart and  everything else so you need to disregard  all that but if you're looking at just  that original with Charlton Heston in it  then yeah this is surprisingly lining up  with everything well and with Nova they  cover the idea of why humans in that  film in that future are mute and don't  speak which wasn't  me I was expecting to be a drug there  wasn't like a boy I hope they fill them  that flat hole but I love that they came  up with a way that felt organic to do it  and yet have recalled Nova which is a  wonderful nod to the original there were  a lot of very cool little nods know who  was one the the crosses that they hang  the I mean they're not really crosses  their exes but the the things that they  hang the Apes up were basically the same  ratings as the Scarecrow's from the  beginning of the Planet of the Apes  movie and there were just these great  wonderful visual or dialogue nods to the  original film because I do love the  original plan of the Apes I love it a  lot I don't want to compare it to these  because I think they're you know just  the style of filmmaking and acting and  everything else is very different this  movie really does a number of things  that I think 