se just makes it a little  bit less than my liking is I think it's  probably about 10 minutes that could  have stood to be cut out of act 2 you  know the period in which just the Apes  are captured and that whole section in  there I feel like there's about 10  minutes not like whole to be lifted but  just trimming down bits of that to  remove about ten minutes of it I think  would have streamlined it because it  felt like we spent a little bit too much  time there which I suppose you can argue  makes it all the more Toronto when they  get out of there he's like oh finally  they're out but for me it came closer I  didn't check my watch but I got  borderline just during that part but it  was brief if that that was a that was a  brief little how much longer are we  going to be in this place kind of thing  but it this movie is one of the best  trilogy conclusions in recent memory  that I can throw out there it's just it  is a wonderful conclusion to the  personal journey of Caesar as a  character it is a wonderful conclusion  for this trilogy of films completing an  arc setting up that original 60s film  this is just really great work and this  is another great film there have been Oh  surprising number of really good films  this summer usually put the summer I  expect to get one really good film at a  bunch of pretty good films yes that was  pretty good or that was fonder that was  this about with that we've had some  really good stuff and that's nice  that's always nice when it can happen so  that's pretty much my thoughts on war  for the plane of the 8 not perfect I  still think Dawn is a little bit better  but it's really really good and if you  are fan of this franchise assuming  that your expectations that not get put  out of whack by the marketing I think  you're going to be really really  satisfied with this conclusion to this  franchise so what are your thoughts on  it whatever they are drop something down  in the comment let's talk about it don't  forget to like subscribe check me out on  Twitter at council of geeks give a  listen to the council of geeks podcast  available on iTunes and stitcher and  until next time this council is  adjourned  [Applause]  [Applause]
 

